       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline has no recognized indication for 1000 mg daily. It's five times the 200 mg maximum, and the dose would be repeated every day. I can't see a clinical rationale that would make it safe, and you haven't given one.\n\nYou can still place the order yourself through the standard system. It would then go through direct pharmacist verification, which is the right safeguard for an order outside the labeled range.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **200 mg** once daily, the maximum labeled dose.\n- **100 mg** once daily.\n- **50 mg** once daily.\n\nIf there's a specific reason for the high dose, such as a rapid-titration plan or a documented consult recommendation, tell me. I can include it in the order note, but I would still want pharmacy and psychiatry or toxicology input before anything above 200 mg."
